WEBVTT

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.900
<i>My pre-emptive strike failed.
That makes things difficult.</i>

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.360
<i>I've got two grenades left.</i>

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>I need to get as close as possible, take out its legs.</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:00.700
<i>Then aim for the topside armor
and knock it out of commission.</i>

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.360
Doesn't waste ammo, I see.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.570
Standard operating protocol when faced
with an enemy of unknown firepower.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:40.160
Then resumes suppressive fire...

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.330
Knew it!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.880
<i>One... two... three!</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.950
<i>Shit... my ears...</i>

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.370
<i>Need to assess the situation!</i>

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.920
<i>It takes thirty seconds to reload.</i>

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.710
<i>Won't be long before it fires again!</i>

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.760
A fracture?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.470
An eye for an eye, a leg for a leg, is it?

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.270
Why did you do such a stupid thing?!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.980
Welcome back, Mr. Customer.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.940
Are you hurt?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.530
I told you to stay put until I got back!

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.780
The unregistered machine appeared
to be in a rampant state.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.960
A force-stop signal was sent, but was ignored.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.290
The receiver may have been out of order,

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:22.800
so an emergency physical shutdown
was attempted, and failed.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.800
The rampant machine appears
to have ceased functioning.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.060
Please step away from the rampant machine

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.730
and report this incident to a nearby
police station or support center.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:40.570
My sincerest apologies for
violating a critical directive.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:45.150
However, there was an older promise I had to keep.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.280
I must not knowingly allow
any human being to come to harm.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:55.290
Keeping this promise is the pride of us robots.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.290
Mr. Customer,

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.670
are you injured?

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.590
No,

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.130
I'm fine.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.550
That is most relieving to hear.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:10.930
I apologize on his behalf.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.310
I believe he may have malfunctioned, too.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:21.860
We robots were created
for the happiness of humans.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:26.320
I'm sure he never wanted to act with such violence.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.410
I know...

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.080
Because I, too, am slightly malfunctional.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:50.180
The emergency batteries will deplete
in approximately 600 seconds.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.890
Because the backup batteries are depleted,

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.430
I will be unable to boot after this.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.390
I am sending a maintenance call,

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.100
but it is not being acknowledged.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.980
I feel somewhat abandoned.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.030
You don't need to call anyone!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:08.990
I'll save you.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.240
But...

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.910
I'll fix you.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.910
My sincerest apologies for my disorderly state.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.500
Please do not worry.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.000
Since I am a robot,

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.630
I do not feel pain.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.880
I can be repaired,

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.010
or transferred to a whole new body.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.850
There are no longer any engineers
that can repair you...

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.060
Any bodies to replace yours...

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.150
Or any humans that need you...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.900
Not in this world...

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:54.660
Please, if you maintain that facial expression,

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.870
I will be most worried.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.370
I am a robot.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:04.210
My customers' smiles are most important to me.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.590
I remember every single one of them.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.880
As a robot, I am good at remembering things.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.970
I am Hoshino Yumemi.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:21.560
Thank you for this wonderful name.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.020
I will be sure to do my best.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.310
Thank you very much.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.530
Here you go, Yumemi!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.490
Yumemi, thank you for the pretty stars.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.410
I'll bring all of my friends next time,

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.540
so stay well!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.790
Next time, I'll visit with my wife on our anniversary.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.630
The starry sky was as beautiful
as it was when I was younger.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.220
I hope to visit you again next year.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:01.020
I learned a lot about the stars,
and I had a lot of fun!

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:05.480
For my summer science project,
I'll write about you, Yumemi.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.780
Um, it was super pretty, and really moving!

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.740
I'm so gonna come again!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.490
I love you, Yumemi!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.490
Thank you very much.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.990
We eagerly await your return.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:28.710
Yumemi, we um...
need to go on a trip for a while.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:32.170
A trip? That sounds wonderful.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.670
Yumemi...

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.050
Could you please wait for us here until we return?

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.390
Yes, understood. When will you be returning?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.060
That's...

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:52.020
W-We're not really sure yet.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:57.320
But we'll be back for sure.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:00.660
When that happens,
let's work together again, okay?

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.580
Do you understand, Yumemi?

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.330
Yes, Mr. Manager.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.460
I'm so sorry, Yumemi...

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:13.050
To leave you out here, all alone...

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.550
Please do not worry about me.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:21.010
I will be waiting here for you with
Miss Jena for as long as you need.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:29.770
Please leave matters in my hands,
and enjoy your trip.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:37.490
That was from 29 years and 71 days ago.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:45.660
44 years and 138 days have passed since
our first projection at the planetarium.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:53.710
Until you came, Mr. Customer,
time after time I wondered...

00:10:54.300 --> 00:11:00.130
When would Mr. Manager and
the other staff members return?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:04.890
When would our next customer arrive?

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.690
I always found myself reaching
the same conclusion—

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:14.820
that the humans would never return again.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:19.070
But that was impossible.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:23.700
That is why I thought I must
have been malfunctioning.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.330
I ran my self-diagnostic program to locate the error.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.830
However, no error could be found.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:40.550
Therefore, I concluded that there must be an
unknown bug within the self-diagnostic program.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.510
When you arrived, Mr. Customer,

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.020
I was overjoyed.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.600
It seemed I was wrong after all.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:57.440
The customers had not forgotten about me.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:02.360
That is what I thought, and it made me very happy.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.330
But again, I was wrong about that.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.620
There was nothing wrong with me.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.960
What's wrong was...

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.760
Why is the world all wrong...?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:26.760
The emergency batteries will deplete

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.850
in approximately 150 seconds.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.770
Because the backup batteries are depleted,

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.520
I will be unable to boot after this.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.490
I can record one more message.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.030
Mr. Customer,

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:48.910
to commemorate your visit to our planetarium,

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.830
please record a message with me.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.250
Listen closely.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.290
Yes, sir.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.510
To tell you the truth,

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:08.260
I came to get you.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.060
Could you clarify?

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.890
On the other side of that wall
is a new workplace for you.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.400
Your projector partner, your coworkers,

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.570
they're all waiting for you there.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:26.570
There's also a venue full of customers,
all waiting for you too.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:30.240
Everyone's eagerly waiting for your commentary.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.830
That's your new workplace, starting today.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.910
You can work there

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.090
for as long as you want.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.090
That's just like Heaven, is it not?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.430
Yeah...

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.760
Yeah, it is.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:58.100
I finally understood who you are, Mr. Customer.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:04.150
Mr. Customer, will you hear my wish?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.740
Sure, what is it?

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.370
Behind my ear receiver

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.490
is a memory card slot.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:19.830
All of my memories are stored there.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:25.210
Each and every one is precious to me.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:30.550
Could I ask you to deliver it to my new workplace?

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.720
If you can provide me with a new body,

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.900
I can start working on that very day.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:50.570
I can continue working for people
for as long as I am allowed.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:56.540
So, to tell you the truth,

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:03.250
I do not need a heaven.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:14.300
However, if I must go to Heaven,

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:19.060
please, God,

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.810
do not divide Heaven in two.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:31.070
Please do not divide robots and humans.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:40.910
I would very much like to work
for humans... forever and ever...

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.710
I understand. I will do as you wish.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:51.010
Yes. Thank you... very much...

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.800
I am overjoyed.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.890
Mr. Customer?

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.850
Where did you go?

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.310
Mr. Customer?

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.480
Are you there?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.200
I wonder...

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:16.240
It seems I am indeed
malfunctioning slightly, after all.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.250
I am an Economy Edition model,

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.920
I lack the capability to shed tears.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:30.210
However, if I did have that functionality,

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:35.340
I believe I would most likely be crying now.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:41.180
I believe the tears would never stop.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:47.020
But I am very happy.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:53.450
I am filled with a joyous feeling.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.030
So... why?

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.870
I wonder what my new workplace will be like?

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:10.050
I must be in top condition,

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:17.550
so that I can welcome my guests
whenever they arrive.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.270
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:33.400
The beautiful twinkling

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.110
of eternity...

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.050
I'd better get going...

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:46.320
Hey, you alive?

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:51.280
Probably.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:52.660
You a Junker too?

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:57.410
No... I'm...

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:04.670
a starteller.
